TASK-315 runtime harness (2026-11-10). Temporary code, never committed to
Detour/. Gated on DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR, DETOUR_DATA_DIR and DETOUR_VERIFY_BASE (a
local server serving audio.html, an <audio autoplay loop> of a 440 Hz WAV,
and links.html, a link plus an <input>). In a second window it runs three
histories, each ending in performClose with only weak references held:

  plain      one page, then close (control)
  pip        a tab really playing audio is left for another tab (the auto
             picture-in-picture path keeps its container as pipContentView)
  inspector  the page's Web Inspector docked (forced with _inspector.attach),
             then another tab

and logs: the link-hover status bar and isEditingWebContent after a scripted
mouseover / focus (the messages still reach the window), which handlers the
left page still has (typeof window.webkit.messageHandlers.*), whether the
controller and the NSWindow are freed, and whether the closed window's number
is still listed off-screen by CGWindowListCopyWindowInfo(.optionAll).

Results: unfixed BrowserWindowController.swift -> pip and inspector LEAKED
(handlers left on the page, window listed off-screen for good); fixed -> all
three FREED. Note: even a freed controller's NSWindow lives until the next
event goes through the queue (AppKit's event-loop autorelease pool; an idle
harness run gets none), so the harness posts an application-defined event 4 s
after the close.

    git apply docs/harness/task315-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug -derivedDataPath .derived build
    (serve the two pages and the WAV on 127.0.0.1:8765, then)
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify315x DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR=$OUT DETOUR_VERIFY_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8765/ \
      .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour
    (wait for "] done" in $OUT/verify-315.log, kill that PID only)
    git apply -R docs/harness/task315-harness.patch && xcodegen generate

